brief:
On the broad paved square beside the twin-towered romanesque minster in the bright afternoon sun, four boys and a huge red dragon stand together in a bright, welcoming group on the pale stone walls' lower midground, leaving the entire top third of the frame completely clear with unbroken blue autumn sky. The preschooler Levin—average build, short wavy light blonde hair, green eyes, wearing a red long-sleeve shirt, green corduroy trousers, and brown lace-up ankle boots—stands smiling on the left. Beside him is the toddler Julian—average build, curly ear-length light blonde hair, blue eyes, wearing a blue zip-up fleece jacket over a white long-sleeve top, grey pull-on trousers, and blue rubber-soled ankle boots. Next stands the preschooler Max—average build, short curly light brown hair, brown eyes, wearing a yellow crew-neck sweatshirt, brown denim dungaree shorts, and white high-top trainers. On the right stands the preschooler Kiaan—average build, short straight dark brown hair with bangs, brown eyes, wearing a green hooded anorak, black jogger trousers, and grey rubber-toe trainers. Funkenherz—the huge dragon with vibrant red scales, a glowing golden scale set in her chest, warm shimmering air rising from her back, and large golden eyes—stands proudly behind them. A few distant passers-by cross the far edge of the square.

